/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  pfr04_adiabatic  --  an ADIABATIC plug-flow reactor.  The temperature is a
                       RESULT, marched with the species by the same RK4:

      dF_i/dV = SUM_j nu_ij r_j(F,T)
      dT/dV   = SUM_j (-dH_j(T)) r_j / SUM_i F_i cp_i(T)

  The esterification is only mildly exothermic in the liquid (dH_rxn about
  -2.7 kJ/mol after the acetic-acid correction,
  docs/design/acetic-acid-latent-heat-closure.md), so the stream warms by only
  6.6 K (356.6 K out, the hot spot is the outlet).  The Arrhenius feedback is
  present but weak.  T(V) is in the axial profile: plot it.

  The original teaching point of this case (positive feedback, a hot spot
  ~100 K above the feed) needs a genuinely exothermic reaction; a replacement
  case on such a reaction is planned.  No parameter was changed.

  `thermalMode` takes `isothermal` (default -- T imposed, duty a result),
  `adiabatic` (here), or `heatExchange` (a jacket: U, areaPerVolume, T_coolant).
  A non-isothermal reactor needs the heat of reaction, so every reacting species
  must carry `standardThermochemistry` -- a fictitious toy species cannot be used.

  The feed is declared at 15 bar, a leftover of the old design (a 454 K
  product had to be held liquid); at the corrected ~357 K the outlet is liquid
  at 1 atm too.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        pfr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( reactorOut );

        operation
        {
            V_R           0.005;        // m^3  (same volume as pfr01)
            nSteps        100;
            thermalMode   adiabatic;    // <-- T is a RESULT (a few K here)
        }
        reactions   ( esterification_etac );   // one-element list -> the general path
    }
);
